.TH "WHATSMYIP.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whatsmyip.sh \- report the publicly observed IPv4 and IPv6 addresses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwhatsmyip.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query ipv4.icanhazip.com and ipv6.icanhazip.com using curl, wget or dig fallbacks. Print IPv4 and IPv6 results separately, displaying Unavailable if either request fails.
.SH NOTES
Addresses are obtained through external network services and may reflect a VPN, proxy, or NAT egress address rather than a local interface.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires outbound network access and one of curl, wget or dig.
It prefers curl, then wget, then dig, for separate IPv4 and IPv6
lookups. DNS, VPN and proxy settings affect the result.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
whatsmyip.sh
curl -4 https://ipv4.icanhazip.com
curl -6 https://ipv6.icanhazip.com
.fi
.SH OPERATION AND TROUBLESHOOTING
The two address families are requested independently. If one
fails it prints Unavailable while still reporting the other.
An IPv6 failure can indicate missing IPv6 routing, not a
problem with IPv4. The reported addresses represent the
remote service's observation of the network egress.
